    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="812eb51f-e853-5bf4-9667-01a8b43dcb2e" activityNameId="f63cbe4f-ade4-5447-a8f1-8e5b9babffac" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Network Attached Storage, NAS, at plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Network Attached Storage, NAS, at plant
The dataset is built from literature, product sheet and internet research; UUID: 1b70f7ea-9758-35c4-aecb-000b694dc3cb
Network attached storage (NAS) is modeled as a small desktop with defined technical specifications of a Synology DS220+ (Synology, 2023). The key technical specifications, which are available in the product datasheet of Synology DS220+, include: CPU Intel Celeron J4025 2-core 2.0 GHz, 2 GB RAM capacity, 4 TB 2.5" HDD storage capacity, system fan, cables, 1 power adaptor, and packaging. The total weight of the modeled NAS is 1.30 kg (without HDDs).
Location: Data for average NAS, applicable for average network storages.
Technology: Typical NAS with the defined technical specifications.
Time period: Unspecified
Production volume: unknown
Sampling: Literature &amp; own estimations
Extrapolations: Average technology
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_1b70f7ea-9758-35c4-aecb-000b694dc3cb.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
